Properties:
   Test run: alr --chdir=test run (from ${CRATE_ROOT}/.)
   Author: Martin Krischik <krischik@users.sourceforge.net>
   Build Switches: 
   Description: AdaCL desktop: Regex and SPITBOL patterns with wide characters
   License: GPL-3.0-or-later
   Long_Description: Regular expression and SPITBOL pattern matching for Ada 2022, with wide character
support.

Features:
- Regular Expressions:
  - Generic implementation for any discrete element array
  - Instantiations for String, Wide_String, and Wide_Wide_String
- SPITBOL Patterns:
  - Pattern construction and matching, inspired by Macro-SPITBOL (Robert Dewar)
  - Supports String, Wide_String, and Wide_Wide_String
- Forked from GNAT.Regexp and GNAT.Spitbol with enhanced wide and wide-wide character support

Licensed under GPL-3.0-or-later. Integrates with the Ada Class Library (AdaCL).

Source: [SourceForge](https://sourceforge.net/p/adacl/git/ci/master/tree/adacl_regexp/)
Documentation:	[Overview](https://adacl.sourceforge.net/adacl-regexp/) and
[GNATdoc](https://adacl.sourceforge.net/gnatdoc/index.html)

   Maintainer: Martin Krischik <krischik@users.sourceforge.net>
   Maintainers_Logins: krischik
   Name: adacl_regexp
   Notes: # Version 8.2.0:
* Updated AdaCL.Trace for better wide-string support
* Added a new line-insert filter to AdaCL.SAR that can insert multiple lines and/or only at the first matched location
* AdaCL.Serial now generates the macOS serial communication layer on the fly

